Impact Model – ET AI Concierge 

 Scope

This impact model reflects the measurable impact of the current working prototype, tested in a controlled/demo environment 

using:

Multi-agent routing system
AI-generated responses (Gemini)
FAISS-based memory
Gradio chatbot interface

 Key Assumptions 

Total test users (demo usage) = 100 users
Avg queries per user = 5
Total interactions = 500 sessions
Manual exploration time (without AI) = 4 minutes/query
AI response time (with system) = ~30 seconds/query

 1. Time Saved (Directly Observable)
Time per query saved:

= 4 min (manual search) – 0.5 min (AI)
= 3.5 minutes saved
Total time saved:
= 500 × 3.5 minutes
= 1750 minutes
= ~29 hours saved (in small-scale test)

2. Conversion Simulation 

Cross-sell agent (premium products)
Marketplace agent (loans, insurance)
CTA-based responses
Assumption (based on interaction behavior):
Users exposed to offers = 300
Estimated engagement rate = 20%
Simulated conversions = 60 users

 Revenue Simulation:

Avg product value = ₹500
= 60 × ₹500
= ₹30,000 simulated revenue (demo scale)

 3. Cost Reduction 

“Which loan?”
“Best investment?”
“Premium options?”

Assumptions:

Queries automated = 200
Cost per human response = ₹10

 Cost saved:
= 200 × ₹10
= ₹2,000 saved

 4. Efficiency Improvement

Before AI:

User navigates multiple pages
No personalization
After AI:
Single chat → full guidance
Context-aware responses (FAISS memory)
Estimated improvement:
Task completion speed ↑ ~70–80%
User effort ↓ significantly

